    "id": 575323,
    "title": "Building a Production-Grade Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) Pipeline",
    "description": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.5867%; height: 519px; border-width: 0px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 20.2037%;\"><col style=\"width: 79.7984%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 152.8px;\">\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; height: 152.8px; border-width: 0px;\">\r\n<p><img src=\"https://events.vtools.ieee.org/vtools.ui/media/display/c29a0ee8-765e-42b9-99ec-75bbf1cff03c\" alt=\"\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"https://events.vtools.ieee.org/vtools_ui/media/display/f37ceeb9-d1f3-4349-ba56-90a3ee88b22c\" alt=\"Nutan_140x140\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt;\"><strong>Nutan Sahoo</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 10pt;\"><strong><img src=\"https://events.vtools.ieee.org/vtools_ui/media/display/c0f0e4ef-8d7f-46a4-8972-5d1c03985c9c\" alt=\"Advitya_140x140\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\"><br>Advitya Gemawat</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 152.8px; border-width: 0px;\"><strong>Description:&nbsp;</strong>Most standard RAG tutorials rely on a naive pattern: splitting text, embedding chunks, and injecting the top matches directly into an LLM prompt. While simple to implement, this approach frequently fails in real-world scenarios, retrieving semantically related but factually irrelevant context, generating unverified assertions, etc. In this hands-on workshop, we move beyond naive RAG to build a robust, production-ready RAG pipeline. Participants will learn how to design resilient architectures that handle complex, domain-specific document.<br>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 2;\"><strong>Key Topics &amp; Implementations Covered:</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0in;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><strong>Structural Document Preprocessing &amp; Chunking:</strong>&nbsp;Parsing hierarchical documents into semantically coherent units rather than arbitrary fixed-character splits.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><strong>Hybrid Search &amp; Retrieval:</strong>&nbsp;Combining sparse keyword matching (BM25) with dense semantic embeddings to capture both exact terminology and conceptual intent.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><strong>Adaptive Feedback Learning:</strong>&nbsp;Integrating dynamic feedback for improving retrieval.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><strong>Sentence-Level In-Line Citations:</strong>&nbsp;Adding verifiable citation tags, so every fact links back to its source document.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><strong>Cross-Session Persistence:</strong>&nbsp;Extracting and storing high-signal user profile facts to maintain continuity across distinct user sessions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>",
